```

Adds Unions to the root Query. 

Given the typeDefs: 

```gql
type Movie {
    title: String!
}

type Series {
    name: String!
}

union Production = Movie | Series
```

You can now query: 

```gql
query {
    productions(where?) {
        ... on Movie {
            title
        }
        ... on Series {
            name
        }
    }
}
````

Based on RFC https://github.com/neo4j/graphql/blob/dev/docs/rfcs/rfc-009-top-level-unions.md

## Notes on implementation
Opted to reuse the `translateRead` function and use individual subqueries over the `union` statement as a subquery is more flexible than a union! There is an extra wrapping `CALL` statement and this is so if one union member MATCH is null the entire query won't exit!

